{ Pade delay approximants. The reads of npd/dpd are deliberate: they give the
  document explicit array syntax, which is what marks it as matrix-carrying for
  tests/matrix_expansion.rs (a bare `[npd, dpd] = pade(...)` encodes its
  array-ness in mangled names only, and that pass would then expect the
  expander to be a no-op on it). }
[npd, dpd] = pade(0.2, 2)
[np3, dp3] = pade(0.5, 3)
lead2 = npd[1] / dpd[1]
lead3 = np3[1] / dp3[1]
